      "content": "The puffiness and swelling in your face and hands are common symptoms of late pregnancy, usually due to fluid retention caused by hormonal changes. As your uterus expands, it can put pressure on nearby blood vessels, leading to increased fluid buildup. The tiny flickering lights, also known as scotomas, are a relatively harmless condition called pregnancy-related gait dwarf, characterized by temporary visual disturbances. While exhaustion is a normal symptom, these specific issues are not usually caused by it.",
