      "content": "While staying hydrated and taking anti-inflammatory pain relievers like ibuprofen may help alleviate some comfort symptoms, it's still recommended to consult your doctor to rule out any potential underlying issues. Swelling, especially if accompanied by vision disturbances, can be a symptom of an underlying condition that requires medical attention. For now, staying hydrated and keeping an ice pack on your face might help reduce puffiness, but don't hesitate to visit your doctor for a thorough checkup and reassurance.",
